{"text": "W\n\n\\\\\n\nPAPER B\n\n_ \\ / Purpose: For Decision\nISLEof\nWIGHT\ncouUN CHL\nCommittee FULL COUNCIL\nDate 20 NOVEMBER 2013\nTitle CONSTITUTION REVIEW - FOLLOWING CONSULTATION\nEXERCISE\nReport of LEADER OF THE COUNCIL\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n1. This report summarises the outcome from the public consultation exercise\nagreed at the September Full Council meeting on the following three options\nfor revised decision making processes of the council:\n(a) | Option 1 - The current one party cabinet with a leader and a separate\nscrutiny function, with no decisions delegated to and made by an\nindividual cabinet member.\n(b) Option 2 - A committee system with committees politically\nproportionate in relation to the representation of political groups on the\ncouncil and one scrutiny committee to meet the statutory scrutiny\nfunctions of health, crime and flooding.\n(c) Option 3 - A hybrid system consisting of a one party executive, with\nfour politically proportionate executive advisory committees and one\nscrutiny committee with the option to set up task and finish groups to\nscrutinise particular issues.\n2. There were 115 responses to the online consultation (a summary is attached\nas Appendix 7) which is a low response and could be seen as statistically\ninsignificant. Of these, 43 per cent preferred option 1, the current system; 36\nper cent preferred option 2, a committee system; and 21 per cent preferred\noption 3 the hybrid executive committee system.\n3. The feedback from the consultation exercise has been considered by the\n\nConstitution Review Working Party. It carefully considered the responses and\ncomments made and agreed that as the consultation response was relatively\nlow, and the outcome is not a significant factor in the decision making\nprocess, although many of the comments made as part of the consultation\nresponses were relevant and were considered as part of the discussions. Its\nrecommendations are:\n\n(a) That given the outcome from the consultation process, and the\npossible impact of implementation of this option on the resources of the\ncouncil, that the committee system (option 2) not be adopted at this\nstage.\n\nB-1",
